<title>BAHRAIN: Saudi's Bank al-Jazira nine-month back in black.</title>
<headline>Saudi's Bank al-Jazira nine-month back in black.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>		(million Saudi riyals unless stated)</p>
<p> Net profit		  11.0	     vs    6.9 loss</p>
<p> Operating income	 172.5	     vs  156.6</p>
<p> Operating expenses     161.9	     vs  163.7</p>
<p> Net operating income    10.5	     vs    7.1 loss</p>
<p> Other income		 0.5	     vs    0.2</p>
<p> Shareholders' funds    518.4	     vs  500.0</p>
<p> Net loans and advances 901.2	     vs    1.40 billion</p>
<p> Deposits		     1.55 billion  vs    1.25 billion</p>
<p> Assets			 3.66 billion  vs    3.88 billion</p>
<p>Full Name: Bank al-Jazira.</p>
<p>Note - The Jeddah-based bank, traded in the Saudi stock market, is 5.83 percent owned by National Bank of Pakistan. The rest is held by Saudi Arabian investors.</p>
</text>
